---
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const url = withBase('/experiments/moonshine-stt/');
const playUrl = withBase('/experiments/play/moonshine-stt/');
const syntheticUrl = withBase('/experiments/moonshine-stt/?synthetic=1');
---

<figure class="moonshine-artifact">
  <iframe
    src={url}
    title="On-device Moonshine speech recognition. Press Load demo before anything is downloaded, then start the microphone."
    sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin"
    allow="microphone"
    loading="lazy"></iframe>
  <figcaption>
    On-device Moonshine Base. Nothing is downloaded until Load demo (~160 MB).
    The first visit is about 160 MB (Base weights plus the runtime). Weights are
    fetched once from Hugging Face and stored in the browser cache. Later visits
    load from that cache. Audio never leaves the device. The demo works best on
    WebGPU. The microphone stays off until a second button. The network panel is
    in the same frame, so it can see this demo's requests.
    <a href={playUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Open a larger view</a
    >.
    <a href={syntheticUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Open with a synthetic source</a
    >. The frame runs scripts and may use the microphone. It keeps this site's
    origin so Cache Storage, WebGPU, module workers, and the directory-scoped
    network service worker can run. An opaque sandbox origin cannot register
    that worker, and Clear site data for this site would not clear its cache.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .moonshine-artifact {
    margin: 36px 0;
  }
  iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 980px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: #fff;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    iframe {
      height: 1280px;
    }
  }
</style>
